<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<WorkflowBuilder Version="2.9.0"
                 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                 xmlns:rx="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Reactive;assembly=Bonsai.Core"
                 xmlns:io="clr-namespace:Bonsai.IO;assembly=Bonsai.System"
                 xmlns:orl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Logging;assembly=OpenRigs.Logging"
                 xmlns:orc="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Core;assembly=OpenRigs.Core"
                 xmlns:cal="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Core.Calibration;assembly=OpenRigs.Core"
                 xmlns:orcl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Control;assembly=OpenRigs.Control"
                 xmlns:lv="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.LiveView;assembly=OpenRigs.LiveView"
                 xmlns:cv="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Vision;assembly=Bonsai.Vision"
                 xmlns:scr="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions;assembly=Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions"
                 xmlns:dev="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Devices;assembly=OpenRigs.Devices"
                 xmlns:vc="clr-namespace:CoenQcCalibrateValve;assembly=Extensions"
                 xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib"
                 xmlns:harp="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Harp;assembly=Bonsai.Harp"
                 xmlns:beh="clr-namespace:Harp.Behavior;assembly=Harp.Behavior"
                 xmlns="https://bonsai-rx.org/2018/workflow">
  <Description>Calibrates the reward valves on a rig's behavior board, one or all of them: fires known pulse widths, weighs what each burst delivers, and writes the weights to calibration\&lt;FileName&gt;-weights.csv beside this machine's rig.yml. All of them is interleaved (Valves, such as RewardValve-Left, RewardValve-Right): each burst is fired on each valve in turn, each weighed before the next, into one container on one balance. It measures only: app-rig-control builds each valve's curve from its rows once the run completes and writes it to that valve's calibration\*.json, where the rig's experiment workflows read it. app-rig-control's Calibrations page launches it with the valves by piece name (Valve or Valves) and FileName; the board's port, each valve's board and line (OpenRigs.Devices WiredRewardValve) and the lick spout stage come from this machine's rig.yml, read into the lab rig model (OpenRigs.Devices ReadLabRig), and every burst is fired on the board's Harp time at the procedure's one pulseGapMs (OpenRigs.Core FirePulses). It sets no clock: it reads the behavior board's time as it runs (ClockFromBoard, SetClock false), which on a dome follows the timestamp generator and elsewhere is the board's own, and times the pulses only against each other on it. The balance is read by eye or off the camera: each weight is given with the Weight command when the weigh metric asks for it. Before it, app-rig-control fires Drip commands (more pulses of the width weighed) until the balance moves, so a drop hanging on the spout falls first; a sample's drip pulses are added to its pulses. The procedure (pulse widths, pulses) is config\valve-calibration.yml, its widths scaled at Go so the smallest is the MinPulseWidthMs parameter (ScaleWidths); before Go, Test commands fire a few pulses at a width so a valve's opening can be seen (TestTrain). The hardware is the lab's device pieces, as in a session (OpenRigs.Devices ReadyGate, BehaviorBoard, ClockFromBoard, PulseOutputs, LickSpoutStage); a calibration has no experiment folder (OpenRigs.Logging NoExperimentFolder), so no piece logs. On a rig whose rig.yml has a lick spout stage, OpenRigs.Devices LickSpoutStage homes it and moves the spouts to rig.yml's lickSpoutDefaultPosition, then both radial axes in (towards the mouse), before Ready, and back to the in position once the last burst is weighed (Extensions\Spouts.bonsai). Ready once the board's time is read, its pulse setup has gone out and the spouts are in; Go runs the procedure; Finished once every burst is weighed.</Description>
  <Workflow>
    <Nodes>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="ConfigRoot" DisplayName="ConfigRoot" Description="The root under which each machine has its own configuration directory, &lt;ConfigRoot&gt;\&lt;RIG&gt;\rig.yml; the weights are written into calibration\ there." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:ReadLabRig.bonsai">
        <Description>This machine's rig.yml (ConfigRoot\&lt;RIG&gt;\rig.yml) read once into the lab rig model: RigConfigs, RigFile and ConfigRoot, which every device piece reads. First, before anything that reads them.</Description>
        <ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</ConfigRoot>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:NoExperimentFolder.bonsai">
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="Valve" DisplayName="Valve" Description="The valve to calibrate, by its piece name, such as RewardValve-Left, when Valves is empty: a RewardValve in rig.yml's wiring on BehaviorBoard-Main. app-rig-control gives it at launch." />
        <Property Name="Valves" DisplayName="Valves" Description="The valves to calibrate together, interleaved, such as RewardValve-Left, RewardValve-Right: each burst fired on each in turn, each weighed before the next, so a run has a burst per valve per sample. Empty: only Valve. app-rig-control gives it at launch for Calibrate All." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Settings</Name>
        <Description>Procedure is config\valve-calibration.yml expanded over the valves (InterleaveValves, src\Extensions): each sample once per valve in Valves (else the one Valve), each found on its line by its piece name in RigConfigs (OpenRigs.Devices WiredRewardValve), in turn, and the priming pulses once per valve, so ManualBalance, RunCalibration and the weights file all follow the bursts as they fire; it stops the workflow if a valve is not a RewardValve on BehaviorBoard-Main in rig.yml or the samples are at different pulseGapMs.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RigConfigs</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="io:ReadAllText">
                <io:Path>..\config\valve-calibration.yml</io:Path>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="cal:DeserializeFromYaml">
              <cal:Type xsi:type="TypeMapping" TypeArguments="cal:DispenseCalibration" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="Valve" DisplayName="Valve" />
              <Property Name="Valves" DisplayName="Valves" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="vc:InterleaveValves">
                
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>Procedure</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="sys:Boolean">
              <rx:Name>SpoutsReady</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="0" To="4" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="4" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="SubjectId" />
        <Property Name="SessionId" />
        <Property Name="LaunchId" Description="The launcher's run id; the launch's own, from app-rig-control." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Initialization</Name>
        <Description>The experiment controller (OpenRigs.Control, ExperimentControl) over TCP 5561, which the rig agent relays. Weight takes each weight read off the balance. Drip fires a drip while a weight is due, published on DripCommands. Reports Recording at Go.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="SubjectId" />
              <Property Name="SessionId" />
              <Property Name="LaunchId" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Control:ExperimentControl.bonsai">
              <SubjectId />
              <SessionId />
              <LaunchId />
              <ControlEndpoint>@tcp://127.0.0.1:5561</ControlEndpoint>
              <Parameters>
                <Parameter>
                  <Name>MinPulseWidthMs</Name>
                  <Value>20</Value>
                  <Description>The shortest pulse width calibrated, in ms, set per rig on app-rig-control's Calibrations page: at Go every width of config\valve-calibration.yml is scaled so its smallest is this (the largest 5 times it), the pulses as written (ScaleWidths).</Description>
                  <Minimum>5</Minimum>
                  <Maximum>100</Maximum>
                </Parameter>
              </Parameters>
              <Commands>
                <Command>
                  <Name>Weight</Name>
                  <Description>The balance's reading, in grams, given when the weigh metric asks for it.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>Drip</Name>
                  <Description>Fires a drip while a weight is due, so a drop hanging on the spout falls before the reading: the text is its pulses, at the width being weighed on its valve (for the baseline, also the valve, such as 1 RewardValve-Right). A sample's drip pulses are added to its pulses.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>Snapshot</Name>
                  <Description>Saves the calibration camera's latest frame, full size, as calibration\runs\&lt;text&gt;.jpg beside rig.yml (app-rig-control gives the text as &lt;kind&gt;\&lt;run&gt;\&lt;still&gt;, so each still lands in its run's folder): app-rig-control's Calibrations page reads the balance from it.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>Test</Name>
                  <Description>Before Go, fires pulses to see a valve open at a width: the text is the width in ms, the pulses and the valve, such as 20 10 RewardValve-Left (TestTrain). Not counted anywhere. At Go the test pulses stop, a train still firing too (TakeUntil after its FirePulses), and later Tests are ignored.</Description>
                </Command>
              </Commands>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportPhase">
                <orcl:Phase>Recording</orcl:Phase>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnCommand">
                <orcl:Name>Drip</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject">
              <Name>DripCommands</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Description>Ends headless Bonsai when it is still running 2 s after the controller's stop: the live view's publisher threads keep the process alive until every device's teardown reaches them, so one held up would keep Bonsai running until the agent's kill; exit code 1 after any other end. Nothing in the editor.</Description>
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:EndAfterStop">
                <orcl:GraceSeconds>2</orcl:GraceSeconds>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Hardware</Name>
        <Description>The rig's pieces, as in a session (lib-open-rigs building-blocks): the Ready gate (ReadyGate), the behavior board BehaviorBoard-Main on rig.yml's port (BehaviorBoard, which clears any ZapitTrigger line however the workflow stops), its time, read and never set (ClockFromBoard, SetClock false: Timestamp, the board's time from its analog data events, 1 kHz, as it runs, following the timestamp generator on a dome and its own elsewhere, which every burst is timed on relative to the others, OpenRigs.Core FirePulses at the procedure's pulseGapMs) and its pulsed lines (PulseOutputs: rig.yml's outputPulseEnable without the ZapitTrigger line, stopping at Start if a RewardValve line is not among them; BehaviorBoard-Main.TriggerCalibratedPulse fires one pulse of a given width on a line). Ready (ReadyGate) once the board's time is read (PieceStages, HarpClockRead, at its first heartbeat), PulseOutputs' setup has gone out (PulsesEnabled: pulse mode and widths on its lines, so a Go cannot fire a pulse on a line not yet in pulse mode) and CalibrationReady, this workflow's own stage (WorkflowStages), has come: the spouts are in (SpoutsReady, Extensions\Spouts.bonsai). The balance is read by eye (OpenRigs.Devices ManualBalance): from Go it asks for each weight in the weigh metric and publishes the one given with the Weight command on BalanceReading. The calibration camera (Pip, 10 Nov 2026) is a USB camera plugged in on the balance, a different one on each rig and in no rig.yml: the piece OpenRigs.Devices UsbCamera (Camera-Balance) opens the first that is not the rig's own and publishes its frames as Camera-Balance.Data, which LiveView streams as a temporary device and Snapshots saves; none plugged in stops the workflow at start, saying so. Nothing is recorded. Its exposure is the piece's Camera-Balance.ExposureUs parameter, starting at 15625 (1/64 s), so app-rig-control's Calibrations page can make the balance's display readable. No gain: a USB camera's has no unit common to its models. No camera trigger runs, so DO0 and DO1 stay free.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:ReadyGate.bonsai">
              <PieceStages>HarpClockRead, PulsesEnabled</PieceStages>
              <WorkflowStages>CalibrationReady</WorkflowStages>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:BehaviorBoard.bonsai">
              <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main</Name>
              <CommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</CommandsSubjectName>
              <DataSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</DataSubjectName>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:ClockFromBoard.bonsai">
              <Board>BehaviorBoard-Main</Board>
              <SetClock>false</SetClock>
              <BoardDataSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</BoardDataSubjectName>
              <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:PulseOutputs.bonsai">
              <Board>BehaviorBoard-Main</Board>
              <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
              <BoardDataSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</BoardDataSubjectName>
              <BoardTriggerCalibratedPulseSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.TriggerCalibratedPulse</BoardTriggerCalibratedPulseSubjectName>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>SpoutsReady</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orc:AnnounceStage">
                <orc:Stage>CalibrationReady</orc:Stage>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>ReadyStages</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject" TypeArguments="orc:WeightMeasurement">
              <rx:Name>BalanceReading</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Procedure</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
              <Name>ManualBalance</Name>
              <Description>A balance read by eye, OpenRigs.Devices ManualBalance. From Go it follows the procedure's bursts by their pulses, on BurstPulses (never a drip's: drips fire on BehaviorBoard-Main.TriggerCalibratedPulse alone, so its count of bursts holds), and, once each has landed, asks for a weight in the weigh metric; the next weight typed with the Weight command is forwarded to BalanceReading as that burst's reading.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnCommand">
                      <orcl:Name>Weight</orcl:Name>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject">
                    <Name>WeightEntries</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>Procedure</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="vc:ScaleWidths" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:ManualBalance.bonsai">
                    <RequestSubjectName>BurstPulses</RequestSubjectName>
                    <EntriesSubjectName>WeightEntries</EntriesSubjectName>
                    <ReadingsSubjectName>ManualReading</ReadingsSubjectName>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                      <orcl:Name>weigh</orcl:Name>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>ManualReading</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
                    <Name>BalanceReading</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ParameterValue">
                      <orcl:Name>MinPulseWidthMs</orcl:Name>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="13" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="13" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="sys:Tuple(sys:String,sys:Int32)">
              <rx:Name>BurstPulses</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnCommand">
                <orcl:Name>Test</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Procedure</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:WithLatestFrom" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="vc:TestTrain" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="InputMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="Line" Selector="Line" />
                <Property Name="PulseWidthMs" Selector="PulseWidthMs" />
                <Property Name="Pulses" Selector="Pulses" />
                <Property Name="PulseGapMs" Selector="PulseGapMs" />
              </PropertyMappings>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Timestamp</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orc:FirePulses">
                <orc:Line>DO1</orc:Line>
                <orc:PulseWidthMs>1</orc:PulseWidthMs>
                <orc:Pulses>0</orc:Pulses>
                <orc:PulseGapMs>0</orc:PulseGapMs>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main.TriggerCalibratedPulse</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RigConfigs</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:WithLatestFrom" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:UsbCamera.bonsai">
              <ExposureUs>15625</ExposureUs>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="13" To="17" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="14" To="15" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="16" To="17" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="17" To="24" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="18" To="19" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="19" To="21" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="20" To="21" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="21" To="15" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="15" To="22" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="23" To="24" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="24" To="18" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="FileName" DisplayName="FileName" Description="The run's file name without extension, such as RewardValve-Left (the valve's piece name, never its line's), or RewardValve-All for every valve together: the weights go to calibration\&lt;FileName&gt;-weights.csv, and app-rig-control writes each valve's curve from them to its own calibration\*.json. app-rig-control gives it at launch." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Calibration</Name>
        <Description>Reports the valves and the weights file as the target metric. At Go, RunCalibration with Procedure (the bursts of OpenRigs.Core's DispenseCalibration, without its fit, expanded over the valves): it primes each valve and weighs a baseline, then fires each burst on its valve through BehaviorBoard-Main.TriggerCalibratedPulse (ValveTrains into FirePulses, on the Harp clock at the procedure's pulseGapMs) and weighs on BalanceReading. Each burst is written as it is weighed to calibration\&lt;FileName&gt;-weights.csv beside rig.yml, RigFile's folder (columns pulseWidthMs, pulses, beforeG, afterG, valve, pulseGapMs: its pulse width in ms, its pulses with the drips fired after it (SampleDrips), the grams before and after it, the valve it fired (RewardValve-Left), and the off-to-on time between its pulses in ms; replaced every run). No fit here: once the run completes, app-rig-control splits the rows by valve, builds each valve's curve and writes it to that valve's calibration\*.json, the one it replaces to calibration\_backups\, refusing one whose fitted line does not rise (a slope of 0 or less) or gives no volume at its shortest width. Reports how many bursts were weighed as the points metric, then Finished. Each weighing is zipped with its drips from SampleDrips, which never completes, so SampleDrips is cut off once RunCalibration's last weighing has passed (Last, TakeUntil): a Zip whose first input has ended still waits for its second, and without the cut the rows never ended, so Finished was never reported (10 Nov 2026: Calibrate All stuck after its last weight).</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="Value" DisplayName="FileName" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="StringProperty">
                <Value>RewardValve-Left</Value>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Procedure</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="vc:DescribeValves" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Format">
              <Format>{0} into calibration/{1}-weights.csv</Format>
              <Selector>Item1,Item2</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>target</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RigFile</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="io:GetDirectoryName" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Format">
              <Format>{0}\calibration\{1}-weights.csv</Format>
              <Selector>Item1,Item2.Item2</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
              <Name>WriteWeights</Name>
              <Description>The weights file, opened only once its path is known: a CsvWriter creates its file when the workflow starts, from whatever FileName it has then, and RigFile (an AsyncSubject) arrives a moment later, so a writer mapped from it directly wrote into the workflow's own folder, the lab clone, every run. Started by the path, it writes the rows CalibrationWeights carries.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="FileName" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>CalibrationWeights</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="orl:CsvWriter">
                    <io:FileName>valve-weights.csv</io:FileName>
                    <io:Append>false</io:Append>
                    <io:Overwrite>true</io:Overwrite>
                    <io:Suffix>None</io:Suffix>
                    <io:IncludeHeader>true</io:IncludeHeader>
                    <orl:AutoFlush>false</orl:AutoFlush>
                    <orl:PublishRows>false</orl:PublishRows>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="3" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Procedure</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="vc:ScaleWidths" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
              <Name>RunCalibration</Name>
              <Description>The bursts of OpenRigs.Core's DispenseCalibration settings, this repository's own steps, with no fit and no file writing: primes each valve and weighs a baseline, then each sample's burst on its valve (ValveTrains, src\Extensions, into OpenRigs.Core FirePulses on the Harp clock) and its weighing, in turn. The settings sit in a scoped subject so every step reads the same values. Output: each burst once weighed, as ((grams after, grams before), its sample).</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
                    <Name>ScaledProcedure</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>ScaledProcedure</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>ScaledProcedure</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="SettleReadings" Selector="Procedure.SettleReadings" />
                      <Property Name="TimeoutSeconds" Selector="Procedure.WeighTimeoutSeconds" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:CreateObservable">
                    <Name>PrimeAndWeighBaseline</Name>
                    <Description>Fires the priming burst to fill the line, then weighs the baseline once it has landed. While it is due, each Drip fires on the valve it names (DripTrains into FirePulses), at the largest sample's width, so each spout's hanging drop falls first; those pulses count nowhere. The priming burst's pulses also go on BurstPulses, which ManualBalance counts; a drip's never do. BurstPulses is a BehaviorSubject: a MulticastSubject passes on its source's completion, which ends a PublishSubject for good, so the priming burst's end would leave ManualBalance deaf to every sample (8 Nov 2026: a run stopped at Firing sample 1).</Description>
                    <Workflow>
                      <Nodes>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                          <Name>Source1</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                          <Selector>Procedure</Selector>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="vc:ValveTrains">
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
                          <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main.TriggerCalibratedPulse</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>BalanceReading</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
                          <Property Name="SettleReadings" />
                          <Property Name="TimeoutSeconds" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="orc:WeighStable">
                            <orc:SettleReadings>10</orc:SettleReadings>
                            <orc:TimeoutSeconds>60</orc:TimeoutSeconds>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>DripCommands</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="vc:DripTrains">
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
                          <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main.TriggerCalibratedPulse</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
                          <Name>BurstPulses</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="InputMapping">
                          <PropertyMappings>
                            <Property Name="Line" Selector="Line" />
                            <Property Name="PulseWidthMs" Selector="PulseWidthMs" />
                            <Property Name="Pulses" Selector="Pulses" />
                            <Property Name="PulseGapMs" Selector="PulseGapMs" />
                          </PropertyMappings>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>Timestamp</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="orc:FirePulses">
                            <orc:Line>DO1</orc:Line>
                            <orc:PulseWidthMs>1</orc:PulseWidthMs>
                            <orc:Pulses>0</orc:Pulses>
                            <orc:PulseGapMs>0</orc:PulseGapMs>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="InputMapping">
                          <PropertyMappings>
                            <Property Name="Line" Selector="Line" />
                            <Property Name="PulseWidthMs" Selector="PulseWidthMs" />
                            <Property Name="Pulses" Selector="Pulses" />
                            <Property Name="PulseGapMs" Selector="PulseGapMs" />
                          </PropertyMappings>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>Timestamp</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="orc:FirePulses">
                            <orc:Line>DO1</orc:Line>
                            <orc:PulseWidthMs>1</orc:PulseWidthMs>
                            <orc:Pulses>0</orc:Pulses>
                            <orc:PulseGapMs>0</orc:PulseGapMs>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>RigConfigs</Name>
                        </Expression>
                      </Nodes>
                      <Edges>
                        <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="2" To="12" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="12" To="14" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="13" To="14" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="14" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="14" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="4" To="6" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source3" />
                        <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="1" To="9" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="9" To="15" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="15" To="17" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="16" To="17" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="17" To="10" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="3" To="11" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="18" To="9" Label="Source3" />
                      </Edges>
                    </Workflow>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>ScaledProcedure</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Procedure.Samples</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Concat" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>ScaledProcedure</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="SettleReadings" Selector="Procedure.SettleReadings" />
                      <Property Name="TimeoutSeconds" Selector="Procedure.WeighTimeoutSeconds" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:CreateObservable">
                    <Name>FireAndWeighSample</Name>
                    <Description>One sample: fires its burst of pulses, then weighs once the last has landed. While it is due, each Drip fires more pulses of its width on its valve (DripTrains into FirePulses), until app-rig-control sees the balance move; the drip pulses fired before the weighing go on SampleDrips, for its row's pulses. SampleDrips is a BehaviorSubject, as each sample's Count completes and would end a PublishSubject after the first sample, and the Zip of rows with it (8 Nov 2026: a run Finished after sample 2 with one row). The burst's own pulses also go on BurstPulses, which ManualBalance counts; a drip's never do. The samples run in turn, each starting after the previous weighing.</Description>
                    <Workflow>
                      <Nodes>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                          <Name>Source1</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="vc:ValveTrains">
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
                          <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main.TriggerCalibratedPulse</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>BalanceReading</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
                          <Property Name="SettleReadings" />
                          <Property Name="TimeoutSeconds" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="orc:WeighStable">
                            <orc:SettleReadings>10</orc:SettleReadings>
                            <orc:TimeoutSeconds>60</orc:TimeoutSeconds>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>DripCommands</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="vc:DripTrains">
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
                          <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main.TriggerCalibratedPulse</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Count" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
                          <Name>SampleDrips</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
                          <Name>BurstPulses</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="InputMapping">
                          <PropertyMappings>
                            <Property Name="Line" Selector="Line" />
                            <Property Name="PulseWidthMs" Selector="PulseWidthMs" />
                            <Property Name="Pulses" Selector="Pulses" />
                            <Property Name="PulseGapMs" Selector="PulseGapMs" />
                          </PropertyMappings>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>Timestamp</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="orc:FirePulses">
                            <orc:Line>DO1</orc:Line>
                            <orc:PulseWidthMs>1</orc:PulseWidthMs>
                            <orc:Pulses>0</orc:Pulses>
                            <orc:PulseGapMs>0</orc:PulseGapMs>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="InputMapping">
                          <PropertyMappings>
                            <Property Name="Line" Selector="Line" />
                            <Property Name="PulseWidthMs" Selector="PulseWidthMs" />
                            <Property Name="Pulses" Selector="Pulses" />
                            <Property Name="PulseGapMs" Selector="PulseGapMs" />
                          </PropertyMappings>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>Timestamp</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="orc:FirePulses">
                            <orc:Line>DO1</orc:Line>
                            <orc:PulseWidthMs>1</orc:PulseWidthMs>
                            <orc:Pulses>0</orc:Pulses>
                            <orc:PulseGapMs>0</orc:PulseGapMs>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>RigConfigs</Name>
                        </Expression>
                      </Nodes>
                      <Edges>
                        <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="1" To="14" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="14" To="16" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="16" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="16" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="3" To="5" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source3" />
                        <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="0" To="8" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="8" To="17" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="17" To="19" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="18" To="19" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="19" To="9" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="5" To="10" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="2" To="13" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="20" To="8" Label="Source3" />
                      </Edges>
                    </Workflow>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Concat" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Concat" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Skip">
                      <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>ScaledProcedure</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Procedure.Samples</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Concat" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                      <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="21" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="21" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="12" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="8" To="11" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="13" To="14" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="13" To="15" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="14" To="15" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="15" To="19" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="16" To="17" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="17" To="18" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="18" To="19" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="19" To="20" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="vc:ValveWeighingRow">
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject">
              <Name>CalibrationWeights</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Count" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Format">
              <Format>{0} bursts weighed</Format>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>points</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportPhase">
                <orcl:Phase>Finished</orcl:Phase>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="sys:Int32">
              <rx:Name>SampleDrips</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>SampleDrips</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Last" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Format">
              <Format>{0}\calibration\{1}-pulses.csv</Format>
              <Selector>Item1,Item2.Item2</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
              <Name>WritePulses</Name>
              <Description>The board's own record of every pulse, beside the weights: each write the behavior board answers, stamped with its clock, to calibration\&lt;FileName&gt;-pulses.csv (OpenRigs.Logging CsvWriter, columns harpTime, register, value; replaced every run). OutputSet is a line set (Value its lines as a number: DO1 = 2048, DO2 = 4096, DO3 = 8192), the start of a pulse as the board did it; PulseDO1 to PulseDO3 the width written just before, in ms. Bursts are timed on the rig's Harp clock (FirePulses); these rows show what the board really fired. Opened once its path is known, as WriteWeights, and closed with the last weighing.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="FileName" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="harp:FilterMessageType">
                      <harp:FilterType>Include</harp:FilterType>
                      <harp:MessageType>Write</harp:MessageType>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="beh:Parse">
                    <harp:Register xsi:type="beh:TimestampedOutputSet" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>new(Seconds as harpTime, "OutputSet" as register, Convert.ToInt32(Value) as value)</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="beh:Parse">
                    <harp:Register xsi:type="beh:TimestampedPulseDO1" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>new(Seconds as harpTime, "PulseDO1" as register, Convert.ToInt32(Value) as value)</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="beh:Parse">
                    <harp:Register xsi:type="beh:TimestampedPulseDO2" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>new(Seconds as harpTime, "PulseDO2" as register, Convert.ToInt32(Value) as value)</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="beh:Parse">
                    <harp:Register xsi:type="beh:TimestampedPulseDO3" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>new(Seconds as harpTime, "PulseDO3" as register, Convert.ToInt32(Value) as value)</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Merge" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>CalibrationWeights</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Last" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="orl:CsvWriter">
                    <io:FileName>valve-pulses.csv</io:FileName>
                    <io:Append>false</io:Append>
                    <io:Overwrite>true</io:Overwrite>
                    <io:Suffix>None</io:Suffix>
                    <io:IncludeHeader>true</io:IncludeHeader>
                    <orl:AutoFlush>false</orl:AutoFlush>
                    <orl:PublishRows>false</orl:PublishRows>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="10" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="12" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="7" To="12" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="9" To="12" Label="Source3" />
                  <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source4" />
                  <Edge From="12" To="15" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="13" To="14" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="14" To="15" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="16" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="16" To="17" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ParameterValue">
                <orcl:Name>MinPulseWidthMs</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="4" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="10" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="13" To="31" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="31" To="15" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="14" To="15" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="16" To="17" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="17" To="26" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="17" To="27" Label="Source1" />
